.PP
While typing, the usual Emacs editing keys work: C-a, C-e, C-k, C-u,
C-w, C-y, Meta-f, Meta-b. Up and Down step through command history.
.SH COMMANDS
/help lists the commands you can use on the current network, grouped by
what they are for, with the views as one row of names to click; C-s
searches it as you type, and Meta-a shows the commands of every feature.
To begin with:
.TP
.B
/talk target
Open a buffer for a channel or nick, joining the channel
.TP
.B
/msg target text
Send a message
.TP
.B
/net id
Choose the current network
.TP
.B
/networks
Every network's state
.TP
.B
/session
The current network's connection
.TP
.B
/status
The client's log, where errors appear
.TP
.B
/connect, /disconnect, /reconnect
Control the current network's connection
.TP
.B
/quote command
Send an IRC command
.TP
.B
/reload
Load new code and configuration, keeping connections
.TP
.B
/quit
Disconnect from every network and exit
.SH VIEWS
Each view has a command of the same name. With the snotice feature and
operator access:
.TP
.B
cliconn, cliexit
Recent connections and exits
.TP
.B
connload, exitload
Connection and exit load per server, and DNS rotations
.TP
.B
bans
K-Lines, D-Lines and kills
.TP
.B
channels
New channels, flooders and spambots
.TP
.B
netcount
Users per address range, and connection watches
.PP
For chat: buffer (the shown buffer) and list (/list results). For
everyone: console (raw IRC traffic), status, networks, session, stats,
help and plugins.
.SH PLUGINS
Plugins are Lua files in ~/.config/\fBsnowcone\fP/plugins, named in the
[plugins] modules setting. A plugin returns a function that receives
the plugin api; the README has an example.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B
SIGUSR1
Reload code and configuration, like /reload.
.TP
.B
SIGINT, SIGTERM, SIGHUP
Quit, as C-c does.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B
~/.config/\fBsnowcone\fP/hub.toml
The hub configuration (or hub.lua, or the file given with \fB--config\fP).
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME replaces ~/.config when it is set.
.TP
.B
~/.config/\fBsnowcone\fP/plugins/
Plugin files and their saved data.
.TP
.B
~/.config/\fBsnowcone\fP/GeoLite2-ASN.mmdb
With the mmdb Lua library installed, used to show the network that
owns each connecting address.
.TP
.B
/usr/share/\fBsnowcone\fP/
The Lua sources of hub.
